WEBVTT

asr-000013
00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:29.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The hearing of the Committee on Finance, Finance Subcommittee G, is hereby called to order.

asr-000014
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:59.060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Our hearing today is the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget of the Department of Agriculture, its attached agencies and corporations. We would like to acknowledge the presence of Senator Erwin Tulfo. And may we now call on our Committee Secretary, Attorney Philip Lina, to acknowledge and place on record our resource persons for today.

asr-000015
00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You have the floor, Attorney Lina.

asr-000016
00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:29.980
Committee Secretary: Good morning, Mr. Chair. Good morning, Senator Tulfo. In attendance in this budget briefing of the Department of Agriculture are the following: Secretary Francisco Tiu Laurel Jr.; Attorney Asis G. Perez, Undersecretary for Policy Planning and Regulations; Engineer Roger V. Navarro, Undersecretary for Operations and Agri-Fisheries Mechanization.

asr-000017
00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:44.780
Committee Secretary: Nora C. Oliveros, Undersecretary for Finance; Carlos C. Carrag, Undersecretary for Inspectorate and Enforcement; Engineer Christopher V. Morales, Undersecretary for Rice Industry Development.

asr-000018
00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:57.020
Committee Secretary: Undersecretary Cheryl Marie Natividad Caballero, Undersecretary for High Value Crops; Constante J. Palabrica, Undersecretary for Livestock.

asr-000019
00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:02.820
Committee Secretary: Ari A. Perez, Undersecretary for Agro-Marine Industrial Systems.

asr-000020
00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:07.680
Committee Secretary: Telma C. Tolentino, Assistant Secretary for Finance,

asr-000021
00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:12.600
Committee Secretary: Daniel Alfonso N. Aitaydi, Assistant Secretary for Logistics,

asr-000022
00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:17.240
Committee Secretary: Atty. Genevieve E. Villicaria-Guivara,

asr-000023
00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:20.680
Committee Secretary: Assistant Secretary for Agribusiness, Marketing and Consumer Affairs,

asr-000024
00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.840
Committee Secretary: and for Legislative Affairs and DLLO,

asr-000025
00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:28.360
Committee Secretary: Atty. Joycel R. Panlilio, Assistant Secretary for High-Value Crops,

asr-000026
00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.440
Committee Secretary: and Saqib Saka and Intellectual Property Rights.

asr-000027
00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:39.040
Committee Secretary: From the Bureaus, Elisir S. Salilig,

asr-000028
00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:41.580
Committee Secretary: Director, Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources.

asr-000029
00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.180
Committee Secretary: From the Department of Budget and Management,

asr-000030
00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:51.020
Committee Secretary: Gemma G. Ilagan, Director for,

asr-000031
00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:53.560
Committee Secretary: from the Commission on Audit,

asr-000032
00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:55.080
Committee Secretary: Viuli Q. Molina,

asr-000033
00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.340
Committee Secretary: Lorelay M. Placido,

asr-000034
00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.500
Committee Secretary: and Velvet Chiqui M. Manalo,

asr-000035
00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:05.320
Committee Secretary: and other invited guests,

asr-000036
00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.440
Committee Secretary: Director Lourdes Aganon,

asr-000037
00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:12.100
Committee Secretary: the DBM Director for Organization,

asr-000038
00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:15.020
Committee Secretary: Position Classification and Compensation Bureau,

asr-000039
00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.360
Committee Secretary: Helen Holgado, also from the same service,

asr-000040
00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.100
Committee Secretary: Timothy Solomon, People's Budget Coalition.

asr-000041
00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:27.040
Committee Secretary: That's all for now, Mr. Chair. Thank you.

asr-000042
00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:27.240
Committee Secretary: Thank you.

asr-000043
00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:32.560
Committee Secretary: Mr. Ken Abante, from the People's Budget Coalition.

asr-000044
00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:33.120
Committee Secretary: Thank you.

asr-000045
00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:38.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you very much, Atty. Phillip, our Comsec.

asr-000046
00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Magandang umaga sa kanilang lahat.

asr-000047
00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:49.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang warning ng pag-asa na posibleng magpatuloy hanggang first half ng 2027

asr-000048
00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang napakalakas na El Niño.

asr-000049
00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:58.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tinataya naman ng DA na maaaring mabawasa,

asr-000050
00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:06.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ng mga 700,000 metric tons ang palay production sa second half ng taon

asr-000051
00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:12.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: dahil sa strong El Nino at iba pang weather-related shocks.

asr-000052
00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:21.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Banta rin ang matinding init at water shortage sa mga livestock, fishpond, at fisheries.

asr-000053
00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:30.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dahil sa mga babalang ito, kailangang paglaanan ng karampatang budget ang irigasyon,

asr-000054
00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:39.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: imbakan ng tubig, gayon din ang paglalaan para sa agarang tulong sa ating mga magsasaka at mangingisda

asr-000055
00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:47.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: na ngayon pa lamang ay pinsala na ang inaabot o nararamdaman o nararanasan.

asr-000056
00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:51.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: By our calculation, ang pagkawala ng 700,000 metric tons

asr-000057
00:10:51.780 --> 00:11:02.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ng palay ay sapat para sa taonang pangangailangan sa bigas ng tinatayang 3.6 million na mga kababayan natin.

asr-000058
00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:16.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Isang mahalagang hakbang para sa buong bansa ang pag-aproba sa P171.3 billion na inilalaan ng Department of Agriculture for 2027.

asr-000059
00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:21.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang national budget na ito ang gagamitin para tuloy.

asr-000060
00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:29.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: na makapagtanim at makapagpangisda ang ating mga magsasaka at mangingisda

asr-000061
00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:37.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: para merong sapat na supply ang ating mga pamilyan at makakayanan ng pamilyang Pilipino ang kanilang susunod na kakainin.

asr-000062
00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:45.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Isipin natin itong budget na parang paghahanda sa isang malaking salu-salu sa hapagkainan.

asr-000063
00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:51.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: At ang iba't ibang ahensya ng DA,

asr-000064
00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:56.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang ating mga kusinero at bawat isa ay may mahalagang tungkulin.

asr-000065
00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:03.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Bigas, gulay, livestock, isda, storage, distribution.

asr-000066
00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:09.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kailangan tiyakin ng DA na iisa ang sinusunod na plano ng lahat.

asr-000067
00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:17.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi problema ang maraming kusinero, problema kapag walang koordinasyon.

asr-000068
00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:21.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kulang-kulang ang mga sangkap at ikanga pagtulong.

asr-000069
00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: O pagdating ng damo, napatay na ang kabayo.

asr-000070
00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:30.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yan ang hamon para kay Secretary ka-tukayo, Kiko Laurel.

asr-000071
00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The urgency is already measurable.

asr-000072
00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:38.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 6.87 billion pesos in drought losses.

asr-000073
00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:45.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Wala pa yung pinaka-impact ng Super El Nino as of September 26.

asr-000074
00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:50.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yet, as of October 6, assistance medyo nagkukulang.

asr-000075
00:12:51.780 --> 00:13:01.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 2.53 million ang natulungan sa target beneficiaries na 11.2 million.

asr-000076
00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:10.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang tanong din, hindi ba dapat dahil limang regyon na ang tinatamaan ng El Nino

asr-000077
00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:19.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: base sa datos ng DA, hindi ba dapat magdeklara na ng National State of Calamity

asr-000078
00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:21.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang ating national government?

asr-000079
00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:33.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Para magkaroon na ng dagdag na suporta at pondo dahil nga narito na ang El Nino.

asr-000080
00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:45.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: If I recall correctly, El Nino is already damaging crops and livelihoods in Region 2,

asr-000081
00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:51.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Region 5, CALABARZON,

asr-000082
00:13:51.780 --> 00:14:01.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: SOCCSKSARGEN, Region 2, and one more, and Region 5.

asr-000083
00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:06.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So that's 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 of 13 regions.

asr-000084
00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:16.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I believe the Executive Department should seriously consider a State of Calamity Declaration

asr-000085
00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:21.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: so that we can better address the challenge.

asr-000086
00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:23.060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: of the Super El Nino.

asr-000087
00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:29.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dapat maging sentro ng 2027 budget ang tubig at irigasyon.

asr-000088
00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:34.060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pero tatalakayin pa rin natin ang iba pang mga issue ng Departamento.

asr-000089
00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:40.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yung underutilized funds in the 2026 budget, agriculture smuggling,

asr-000090
00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:48.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: agri-impact ng tuloy-tuloy pa rin gulo sa gitnang silangan, ang Iran-US-Israel war,

asr-000091
00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:50.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang taripa sa ating...

asr-000092
00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:59.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: pork imports, mga farm-to-market roads, yung problema sa delay.

asr-000093
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: sa pag-implementa ng food hubs, among others.

asr-000094
00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pakinggan po natin ang presentasyon.

asr-000095
00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:15.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Secretary Kiko, for your presence and your leadership in the Department of Agriculture.

asr-000096
00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:19.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We are ready to hear your presentation.

asr-000097
00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:26.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But before that, we give the floor to Senator Erwin Tulfo for his opening statement.

asr-000098
00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000099
00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:39.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ah, mahal na Chairman, Senator Kiko Pangilinan, si Agriculture Secretary Kiko Laurel, Jr.,

asr-000100
00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:44.540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: mga kasamahan sa pamahalaan, mga kababayan, magandang umaga po sa ating lahat.

asr-000101
00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:48.980
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ngayong araw, ating tatalakay ng panukalang budget ng Department of Agriculture

asr-000102
00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:54.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: at ng mga attached agencies and corporations nito para sa taong 2027.

asr-000103
00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:59.100
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Agrikultura po ay isa sa pinakamahalagang sektor ng ating ekonomiya.

asr-000104
00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Dito, nakasalalay po ang ating pagkain, kabuhayan, ng milyong-milyong magsisakat,

asr-000105
00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:08.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: mangingisda, at sa presyo ng pagkain sa hapag ng bawat Pilipinong pamilya.

asr-000106
00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:17.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Under the 2027 NEP, the DA family has proposed total budget of around 198.4 billion pesos,

asr-000107
00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:23.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: composed approximately of 196.9 billion pesos in new appropriations

asr-000108
00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:26.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and 1.5 billion pesos in automatic appropriations.

asr-000109
00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.640
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Under House Bill No. 108.58,

asr-000110
00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:37.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: itinaas po ito sa 210 billion pesos with 208.5 billion in new appropriations.

asr-000111
00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:42.120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Sa pagginig po nating umaga, nais nating malinawan sa ilang mahalagang usapin.

asr-000112
00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.720
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Una, ang agricultural smuggling.

asr-000113
00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:50.460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Noong nakarang taon, nasaksihan natin ang ating mga hearings sa pangunguna nga po

asr-000114
00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:53.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: ng ating chairman, Sen. Kiko Pangilinan,

asr-000115
00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:58.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: kung paano po nagturuan ng DA, Bureau of Customs, at ilang law enforcement agencies.

asr-000116
00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:05.180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kung sino ang pananagutan sa paghawak, pag-iingat, at pag-dispose o pagsira

asr-000117
00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:08.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: ng mga nakumpiskang smuggled agricultural products.

asr-000118
00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:14.560
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Nalinaw na po ba kung saan nagsisimula at nagtatapos ang mandato ng bawat ahensya?

asr-000119
00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:22.540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: May malinaw na ba ang chain of custody at accountability upang hindi na maulit pang muli ang ganitong kalituhan?

asr-000120
00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:27.540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ikalawa, ang karapatan po ng ating maliliit na mangingisda.

asr-000121
00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:37.780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Naging malaking usapin din po sa 2023 decision ng RTC Malabon sa kaso ng Mercedar Fishing Corporation

asr-000122
00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:45.560
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: na may malaking implikasyon sa pagpasok ng commercial fishing vessels sa 15-kilometer municipal waters.

asr-000123
00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:51.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Isa sa mga nakitang problema rito ay ang procedural lapses ng BIFAR.

asr-000124
00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:58.720
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kagagaling ko lamang po sa Mimaropa kahapon, sa Marinduque, Romblon, Mindoro, at Palacios.

asr-000125
00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:02.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Inawan, iisa po ang sigaw ng mga magsasaka o mangingisda.

asr-000126
00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:10.360
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Wala na pong nakukuhang isda dahil kinuha na po ng malaking kumpanyang ito ang kanilang dapat sana ihuli.

asr-000127
00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:14.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: They are being forced to go out.

asr-000128
00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:18.220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Milya-milya po ang layo para lamang makakuha ng isda.

asr-000129
00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:24.580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Samantalang, ang mga fishing companies, ito, corporation na ito, ay hindi na kailangan lumayo pa

asr-000130
00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:28.720
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: para ikang mangisda at makakuha ng maraming isda.

asr-000131
00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:39.660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ang tanong natin, ano ang ginagawa ng BIFAR upang maitama ang mga pagkukulang at maprotektahan ang kabuhayan ng mga maliliit nating mangingisda?

asr-000132
00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:42.580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ay katlo, rice production.

asr-000133
00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:44.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Tayo ay isang agricultural country.

asr-000134
00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:47.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Dito po matatagpuan ang International Rice Research Institute.

asr-000135
00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:53.460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ngunit nananatili tayong number one importer ng bigas sa buong mundo.

asr-000136
00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:57.660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: During Marshall Law po, tayo po ay exporter.

asr-000137
00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:59.700
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ngayon, tayo na po ang importer.

asr-000138
00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Hindi ba't malaking kabalintunaan ito?

asr-000139
00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:07.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: May lupa tayo, may mga magsasaka, may teknolohiya at mga eksperto.

asr-000140
00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:12.520
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ngunit, bakit hindi pa rin natin matugunan ang sarili nating pangangailangan sa bigas?

asr-000141
00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:17.960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kailangan pa natin, ikanga, humingi ng tulong at kumuha sa ibang bansa.

asr-000142
00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:26.600
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ano ang konkretong plano po ng DEA umang mapataas ang lokal na produksyon at mabawasan ang ating pagdidepende sa importasyon?

asr-000143
00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:40.860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ikaapat, ang kalagayan po ng ating mga magsasaka, marami pong lumalapit sa aming tanggapan na nagre-reklamo sa napakamahal na presyo ng abono at napakamababang farmgate price ng palay.

asr-000144
00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:51.860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Habang hirap na hirap kumita ang ating magsasaka, may mga middlemen at negosyanteng nagpapatong ng napakalaking tubo bago makarating ang produkto sa ating mga mamimili.

asr-000145
00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:55.940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Dalawang beses na talo ang Pilipino.

asr-000146
00:19:55.940 --> 00:20:01.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Lugi na nga po ang magsasaka natin, mahal pa ang binibili ng consumer.

asr-000147
00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:07.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ano ang ginagawa po ng ating ahensya upang mapababa ang production cost?

asr-000148
00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:11.920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Matiyak ang makatarungang presyuhan sa supply chain.

asr-000149
00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:18.580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: At ang ikalamang problema, ang paghahanda sa napipintong matinding El Niño sa susunod na taon.

asr-000150
00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:25.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Hindi natin kailangang antayin matuyo ang ating mga sakahan, masira ang mga pananim.

asr-000151
00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:28.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Tumaas ang presyo ng pagkain bago tayo kumilos.

asr-000152
00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:32.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: May sapat na ba tayong plano para sa irigasyon at patubig?

asr-000153
00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:39.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Nakapaghanda na ba tayo ng drought-resistant crops, mga binhi at iba pang suporta para sa ating mga magsasaka?

asr-000154
00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:45.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Paano natin titiyaking hindi mauwi sa kakulangan ng pagkain ang matinding tagtuyo?

asr-000155
00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:55.060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Sa ating mga kaibigan sa DA, nais ko pong idein na huwag sana natin gawing palaging dahilan ng kakulangan sa budget.

asr-000156
00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kung bakit hindi natin nagagampana ng ating mga tungkulin.

asr-000157
00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:04.900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Taon-taon po, suportado po kayo ng ikang institusyon na ito.

asr-000158
00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:10.360
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Bilyong-bilyong piso po ang inilalaan ng pamahalaan sa sektor po ng agrikultura.

asr-000159
00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:19.120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Karapatan din po ng taong bayan na malaman kung saan napupunta ang pondong ito, paano ito ginagastos at ano ang kongkretong resulta.

asr-000160
00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:25.360
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Hindi po sapat na mataas lang ang utilization, obligation at disbursement rates.

asr-000161
00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:34.060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ang mahalagang tanong ngayon ay may napapala ba ang ating mga magsasaka, mangingisda at mamimili?

asr-000162
00:21:34.780 --> 00:21:39.280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ito po ay isang hamon sa aking kaibigan, si Sekretary Kiko Laurel Jr.

asr-000163
00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:47.220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Sa madaling salita na is natin makita, hindi lamang ang mga programa at pangako, kundi ang mga resulta at malinaw na pananagutan.

asr-000164
00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:55.260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Patunay po natin o patunayan po natin sa ating mga kababayan na ang bawat piso ang inilalaan sa agrikultura ay nagagamit ng tama,

asr-000165
00:21:55.260 --> 00:22:00.840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: fordoktibo at may buong transparency at accountability. Maraming salamat po, Ginong Chairman.

asr-000166
00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:13.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Maraming salamat, Senator Erwin Tulfo. We now give the floor to Sekretary Kiko Laurel. Do you have an opening statement? Go ahead, Sek Kiko, you have the floor.

asr-000167
00:22:13.820 --> 00:22:20.120
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Honorable Chairman, distinguished members of the Senate Committee on Finance, colleagues, ladies and gentlemen, good morning.

asr-000168
00:22:20.640 --> 00:22:25.120
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Today we seek your support for the Department of Agriculture's proposed 2027 Bill.

asr-000169
00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:41.540
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At the time when our farmers and fisherfolk face a perfect storm, a looming super El Nino, worsening climate risks, and rising costs of fuel fertilizers and vital inputs, pressures compounded by geopolitical shocks beyond our control.

asr-000170
00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:51.020
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: The Department of Agriculture cannot control the weather or the price of oil halfway around the world, which also affects the price of fertilizers.

asr-000171
00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:54.800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But we can decide on how prepared our farmers are.

asr-000172
00:22:55.260 --> 00:23:04.000
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And we must. We cannot demand cheap food while leaving farmers struggling to afford to produce it.

asr-000173
00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:12.980
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Nor can we expect our fisherfolks to keep feeding the nation if doing so means their families remain hungry for a better life.

asr-000174
00:23:13.840 --> 00:23:19.940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Affordable food begins with viable farms. Food security begins with secure livelihoods.

asr-000175
00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:24.920
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Our proposed budget is designed to turn these principles into action.

asr-000176
00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:36.700
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: We will continue raising productivity through quality seeds, better inputs and modern technologies, expand farm-to-market roads, cold chain systems, and post-harvest facilities,

asr-000177
00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:43.460
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: and strengthen links between producers and markets so farmers and fisherfolks earn more from what they produce.

asr-000178
00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:49.540
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: We will also invest in climate resilience, disaster preparedness, and biosecurity.

asr-000179
00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:54.400
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Because every harvest lost to drought, every fish catch spoiled in transit,

asr-000180
00:23:55.260 --> 00:24:03.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: every crop destroyed by disease is not merely an agricultural setback, it is food lost, income lost, and opportunity lost.

asr-000181
00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:08.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Every peso invested wisely in agriculture can help deliver more than food.

asr-000182
00:24:08.200 --> 00:24:17.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: It can mean more stable prices, stronger rural economies, better paying livelihoods, and greater dignity for millions of Filipinos.

asr-000183
00:24:17.200 --> 00:24:21.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But public investment must come with public accountability.

asr-000184
00:24:21.200 --> 00:24:25.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Government assistance must reach small farmers, fisherfolks, and agrarian communities.

asr-000185
00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:27.120
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: For whom it is intended.

asr-000186
00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:33.060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Every program must be measured not simply by how much it spends, but by what it delivers.

asr-000187
00:24:33.500 --> 00:24:39.580
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Higher productivity, higher net incomes, fewer post-harvest losses, and food that remains safe and affordable.

asr-000188
00:24:40.860 --> 00:24:47.900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: In a moment, Undersecretary Aziz Perez will present the details of our proposed budget and investments that will help us meet these goals.

asr-000189
00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But beyond the figures lies a fundamental choice.

asr-000190
00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:54.560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Whether we will continue asking our food producers to do more,

asr-000191
00:24:55.260 --> 00:24:59.260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: or give them the tools, infrastructure, and protection they need to thrive.

asr-000192
00:24:59.260 --> 00:25:01.260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Honorable Senators,

asr-000193
00:25:01.260 --> 00:25:05.260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: A nation cannot eat budget figures, but with the right investments,

asr-000194
00:25:05.260 --> 00:25:11.260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: those figures can help put food on every table and a better future within every farmer's reach.

asr-000195
00:25:11.260 --> 00:25:18.260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: On behalf of the Department of Agriculture, I respectfully seek the Senate's support for our proposed 2027 budget.

asr-000196
00:25:18.260 --> 00:25:23.240
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Together, we are committed to a culture that not only feeds the country,

asr-000197
00:25:23.240 --> 00:25:25.240
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: but also provides a more sustainable future.

asr-000198
00:25:25.260 --> 00:25:29.260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: A future that will be more productive and a better life for the people who feed us.

asr-000199
00:25:29.260 --> 00:25:31.260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Thank you very much.

asr-000200
00:25:31.260 --> 00:25:33.260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Thank you Mr. Chairman and good morning to everybody.

asr-000201
00:25:33.260 --> 00:25:37.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you very much, Secretary Kiko Laurel.

asr-000202
00:25:37.260 --> 00:25:43.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Before we get on with the presentation by Usec Aziz Perez,

asr-000203
00:25:43.260 --> 00:25:53.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: we place on record and acknowledge the presence of our former Senate President, currently Senate President Pro Temp, Senator Tito Soto.

asr-000204
00:25:53.260 --> 00:25:54.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, sir.

asr-000205
00:25:55.260 --> 00:26:05.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead, Usec Aziz, with your presentation of the Department's 2027 proposed budget.

asr-000206
00:26:05.260 --> 00:26:07.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Go ahead.

asr-000207
00:26:07.260 --> 00:26:11.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Good morning, Mr. Chair and to the honorable members of this committee.

asr-000208
00:26:11.260 --> 00:26:21.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: It is an honor to present the Department's Agriculture FYI, FY2027 National Expenditure Program.

asr-000209
00:26:21.260 --> 00:26:24.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Before that, I would like to provide the outline of this presentation.

asr-000210
00:26:24.260 --> 00:26:30.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Before you proceed, we'd like to acknowledge the presence of our Senate President,

asr-000211
00:26:30.260 --> 00:26:33.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Senator Win Gatchalian and Senate President Gatchalian.

asr-000212
00:26:33.260 --> 00:26:34.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Good morning.

asr-000213
00:26:34.260 --> 00:26:35.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead.

asr-000214
00:26:35.260 --> 00:26:43.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: In this outline, before we dive into the details of the National Expenditure Program,

asr-000215
00:26:43.260 --> 00:26:50.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: we would like to provide a brief snapshot of the current situation in agriculture and fisheries sector.

asr-000216
00:26:50.260 --> 00:26:56.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This will provide a broader context of our programs and investments under the NEP.

asr-000217
00:26:56.260 --> 00:27:00.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: After this overview, we will walk through the details of the NEP.

asr-000218
00:27:02.260 --> 00:27:19.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Of the 2.3 trillion GDP in 2025, agriculture and fisheries sector generated around 1.83 trillion, contributing around 7.9% to the overall economy.

asr-000219
00:27:20.260 --> 00:27:32.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: The agriculture and fisheries share has steadily declined from 10.1% in 2020 despite remarkable resilience during the pandemic.

asr-000220
00:27:32.260 --> 00:27:39.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This highlights the need to accelerate growth and strengthen the sector's contribution to the economy.

asr-000221
00:27:39.260 --> 00:27:48.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: In terms of stakeholders, we have 10.44 million registered individuals in our SPSA.

asr-000222
00:27:48.260 --> 00:27:56.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This is broadly consistent with the PSA estimate of 10 million people engaged in agriculture and fisheries,

asr-000223
00:27:56.260 --> 00:28:01.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: or an equivalence of about one for every five workers.

asr-000224
00:28:01.260 --> 00:28:06.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Our registry will provide a clearer picture as shown in the table.

asr-000225
00:28:07.500 --> 00:28:19.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Now, poverty among the farmers and fisher folks has declined substantially over the past two decades.

asr-000228
00:28:19.260 --> 00:28:24.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Yet, it remains significantly higher than the national average.

asr-000229
00:28:24.260 --> 00:28:35.740
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: In 2023, poverty incidence stood at 27% for our farmers and 27.4% for our fisher folks, compared with 15.5% nationwide.

asr-000230
00:28:35.740 --> 00:28:40.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This indicates that while we have made progress,

asr-000231
00:28:40.260 --> 00:28:49.020
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: this has yet to be fully translated into improved livelihoods on those sectors who depend on agriculture.

asr-000234
00:28:50.260 --> 00:28:54.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Now, looking deeper into this figure,

asr-000235
00:28:54.260 --> 00:29:01.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: the 7.9% reflects only the value of production at the farm gate,

asr-000236
00:29:01.260 --> 00:29:10.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: but not the much greater value generated when agricultural products are processed, transported, and sold to the market.

asr-000237
00:29:10.260 --> 00:29:12.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Consider this.

asr-000238
00:29:12.260 --> 00:29:16.310
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: There will be no 55 kilogram of rice in Metro Manila without the palay,

asr-000240
00:29:16.310 --> 00:29:20.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: brought at 19 pesos from the farmers.

asr-000241
00:29:20.260 --> 00:29:31.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: There will be no 366 peso per kilogram liempo if there is no pork produced at 170 pesos per kilogram.

asr-000242
00:29:31.260 --> 00:29:37.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: There will be no 206 per kilogram chicken without broiler.

asr-000243
00:29:37.260 --> 00:29:42.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: The chicken produced at 119 peso per kilogram.

asr-000244
00:29:42.260 --> 00:29:45.260
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: These figures highlight the important question.

asr-000245
00:29:45.260 --> 00:29:53.580
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Are we adequately recognizing the contribution of our farmers and fisher folks to the value generated across the economy?

asr-000248
00:29:55.300 --> 00:30:07.640
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: We saw the sector importance during the 2020 pandemic when its share in GDP rose to 10.1%, largely because other sectors contracted more sharply.

asr-000258
00:30:07.640 --> 00:30:14.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: When we look at this sector, share in GDP,

asr-000259
00:30:14.120 --> 00:30:20.880
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: therefore, there is a risk at overlooking agriculture and fisheries in the economic priorities.

asr-000260
00:30:21.880 --> 00:30:26.380
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: It bears to emphasize that agriculture is the foundational industry.

asr-000261
00:30:26.380 --> 00:30:33.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This is a bedrock upon which many other industries and economic activities depend.

asr-000262
00:30:34.020 --> 00:30:39.500
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Investing in agriculture, therefore, is not merely investing in the farmers and the fisherfolk.

asr-000263
00:30:39.500 --> 00:30:44.720
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: It is investing in the strengths, resiliency, and growth in the Philippine economy.

asr-000264
00:30:45.920 --> 00:30:51.500
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: As we have seen so far, agriculture and fisheries sector creates value,

asr-000265
00:30:51.720 --> 00:30:55.560
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: yet food insecurity and poverty and vulnerability

asr-000268
00:30:56.380 --> 00:30:58.300
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: yet food insecurity and poverty and vulnerability exist among the sector.

asr-000269
00:30:59.400 --> 00:31:04.520
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: These persistent challenges can be faced to fundamental bottlenecks

asr-000270
00:31:04.520 --> 00:31:07.880
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: across the agriculture and fisheries value chain,

asr-000271
00:31:08.560 --> 00:31:15.000
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: beginning at the resource level where agricultural land is becoming increasingly fragmented,

asr-000272
00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:25.700
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: with an average size failing from 3.59 hectares to just 0.82 hectares.

asr-000273
00:31:25.700 --> 00:31:36.740
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This suggests that the only way to move forward is to cluster these farms into economic enterprise

asr-000274
00:31:36.740 --> 00:31:40.940
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: to allow what we call the economies of scale.

asr-000275
00:31:41.880 --> 00:31:48.040
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: At the production level, high input costs and low mechanization continue to constrain productivity,

asr-000276
00:31:48.040 --> 00:31:55.040
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: with major commodities falling short of their 2025 PDP.

asr-000277
00:31:55.700 --> 00:32:03.240
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: At the post-harvest stage, we continue to lose significant share of what we produce.

asr-000278
00:32:04.160 --> 00:32:16.860
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Losses reach 14.5% for rice, 31.6% for onion, and 26.5% for mangoes, as an example.

asr-000279
00:32:16.860 --> 00:32:25.680
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This shows that the challenge is not only how to produce more, but to prevent losses and preserve them.

asr-000280
00:32:25.680 --> 00:32:28.360
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: We need to increase the value of production all the way to the market.

asr-000281
00:32:29.220 --> 00:32:37.700
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Finally, logistics and market access remain constrained by inadequate infrastructure and weak transport system.

asr-000282
00:32:38.840 --> 00:32:45.360
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: An estimated 55,050 km gap in farm-to-market access

asr-000283
00:32:45.360 --> 00:32:55.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and 68,433-pallet [unclear] deficit in cold storage capacity

asr-000284
00:32:55.080 --> 00:32:55.660
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: to continue to

asr-000285
00:32:55.680 --> 00:33:02.240
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: raise transport costs, increase losses, and limit farmers' access to market.

asr-000286
00:33:04.920 --> 00:33:11.320
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: As mentioned by the Secretary, as if the challenge continues,

asr-000287
00:33:12.920 --> 00:33:18.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: along with this existing challenge, the impact on the conflict in the Middle East,

asr-000288
00:33:19.660 --> 00:33:24.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: particularly on fuel and fertilizer, has increased drastically.

asr-000289
00:33:25.680 --> 00:33:35.340
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: A year-to-year comparison of August National Weighted Average of Fertilizer will show

asr-000290
00:33:35.340 --> 00:33:42.660
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: a higher prices of 6 out of 7 major grades used.

asr-000291
00:33:43.500 --> 00:33:51.880
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: The highest percentage increase among these includes 46.7% for granular urea,

asr-000292
00:33:51.880 --> 00:33:54.880
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: 43.61% for oil,

asr-000293
00:33:55.680 --> 00:34:03.460
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and 40.89% for pilled urea.

asr-000294
00:34:03.460 --> 00:34:08.120
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: So ito po yung mga figures, sobrang laki na po ng itinaas.

asr-000295
00:34:09.860 --> 00:34:15.940
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Fertilizer prices began rising in the late 2020 as demand recovered from COVID-19,

asr-000296
00:34:16.520 --> 00:34:21.680
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: while supply chain remained disrupted and energy cost increased.

asr-000297
00:34:22.780 --> 00:34:23.460
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000298
00:34:25.680 --> 00:34:30.680
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: The prices.

asr-000299
00:34:30.960 --> 00:34:34.580
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Okay, next slide, next slide.

asr-000300
00:34:34.760 --> 00:34:35.940
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Okay, that's okay.

asr-000301
00:34:38.940 --> 00:34:40.660
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: We go to the farmgate prices.

asr-000302
00:34:40.800 --> 00:34:45.620
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: We have already expounded on the price of fertilizer and fuel.

asr-000303
00:34:45.620 --> 00:34:53.960
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Now we go to, well, contrasting the cost of production is the year-on-year.

asr-000304
00:34:53.960 --> 00:34:54.060
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Okay.

asr-000305
00:34:54.060 --> 00:34:55.160
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Next slide, please.

asr-000306
00:34:55.160 --> 00:34:55.460
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Okay.

asr-000307
00:34:55.460 --> 00:35:02.100
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Go back to the previous slide right after the, okay.

asr-000308
00:35:04.580 --> 00:35:10.980
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Now, notwithstanding the cost or the increase in production cost this year,

asr-000309
00:35:12.280 --> 00:35:19.940
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: a year-on-year comparison of June farmgate prices in selected commodities show varying price changes.

asr-000310
00:35:19.940 --> 00:35:24.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: There is a notable increase in dry palay.

asr-000311
00:35:25.460 --> 00:35:26.160
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: In bangus.

asr-000312
00:35:26.160 --> 00:35:32.160
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: But we further noted a decrease in prices in hogs.

asr-000313
00:35:33.280 --> 00:35:34.580
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: It's 19%.

asr-000314
00:35:34.580 --> 00:35:38.400
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: In red onion, 69%.

asr-000315
00:35:38.400 --> 00:35:40.180
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: In broiler, 9%.

asr-000316
00:35:40.180 --> 00:35:44.320
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Chicken eggs, 7%.

asr-000317
00:35:44.320 --> 00:35:46.280
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: And tilapia, 3%.

asr-000318
00:35:46.280 --> 00:35:52.980
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: So tumataas po yung cost of production, pero generally bumababa po yung presyo at the farmgate level.

asr-000319
00:35:52.980 --> 00:35:53.300
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Okay.

asr-000320
00:35:53.300 --> 00:35:57.860
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Particularly for hogs at this time.

asr-000321
00:35:59.940 --> 00:36:07.700
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: The agricultural sector recorded a trade deficit of around 11.12 billion in 2025.

asr-000322
00:36:09.940 --> 00:36:15.640
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: But it represents a modest improvement of about 5% compared to the previous year.

asr-000323
00:36:16.740 --> 00:36:22.300
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This aligns with the trend observed in 2022 where trade gaps are gradually narrowing.

asr-000324
00:36:22.300 --> 00:36:22.820
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Narrowing.

asr-000325
00:36:23.300 --> 00:36:27.900
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Supported by raising export alongside moderate import growth.

asr-000326
00:36:27.900 --> 00:36:33.020
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Despite this encouraging developments, the trade deficit remains substantial.

asr-000327
00:36:33.760 --> 00:36:43.700
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Bringing this gap will require sustained support for export expansion while aggressively bolstering local farm yields and domestic supply chain.

asr-000328
00:36:48.020 --> 00:36:51.540
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Looking at the composition of agricultural trade,

asr-000329
00:36:51.540 --> 00:36:52.540
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: export remains substantial.

asr-000330
00:36:53.300 --> 00:36:57.300
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: It remains heavily concentrated on just a few commodities.

asr-000331
00:36:57.300 --> 00:37:08.300
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Coconut products lead toward the average of about 3.6 billion, followed by bananas, at 1.68 billion.

asr-000332
00:37:08.300 --> 00:37:17.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Incidentally, Mr. Chair, we are now confirmed as the second biggest exporter of banana in the world.

asr-000333
00:37:17.080 --> 00:37:23.500
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: And pineapple products, around 3.370 million.

asr-000338
00:37:24.400 --> 00:37:29.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: On the import side, animal and vegetable oils and pot account for the largest,

asr-000339
00:37:29.820 --> 00:37:32.780
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: followed by fruits and vegetables and animal feeds.

asr-000340
00:37:32.780 --> 00:37:38.620
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Together, these figures underscore the sector's narrow export resilience,

asr-000341
00:37:39.700 --> 00:37:50.100
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: reliance and on the handful products alongside substantial widespread demand for foreign food items at critical production inputs.

asr-000342
00:37:52.020 --> 00:37:52.900
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Now,

asr-000343
00:37:53.220 --> 00:37:57.400
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Let me bring you to the sufficiency level of selected commodities.

asr-000344
00:37:58.280 --> 00:38:02.320
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Based on the 2025 self-sufficiency level,

asr-000345
00:38:03.420 --> 00:38:06.800
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: domestic production is sufficient in several commodities,

asr-000346
00:38:07.160 --> 00:38:10.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: including root crops and vegetables.

asr-000347
00:38:11.200 --> 00:38:20.360
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: However, there remains a significant gap for rice, potato, onion, coffee, mango, garlic,

asr-000348
00:38:20.360 --> 00:38:23.900
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: indicating continued reliance on imports.

asr-000349
00:38:29.060 --> 00:38:31.160
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: At the livestock level,

asr-000350
00:38:32.260 --> 00:38:36.240
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: livestock and poultry show generally strong domestic production

asr-000351
00:38:36.240 --> 00:38:40.780
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: with chebon and eggs at 100% sufficiency.

asr-000352
00:38:41.840 --> 00:38:45.100
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Chicken and duck's meat are close to self-sufficiency,

asr-000353
00:38:45.100 --> 00:38:47.920
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: while caribbean, pork, beef,

asr-000354
00:38:49.240 --> 00:38:50.300
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: you know, import mix,

asr-000355
00:38:50.360 --> 00:38:53.400
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: are a large supply of these commodities.

asr-000356
00:38:53.640 --> 00:38:56.900
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: For fisheries, we have crabs, oysters,

asr-000357
00:38:58.140 --> 00:39:00.620
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: but when it comes to milkfish, tilapia,

asr-000358
00:39:01.100 --> 00:39:03.020
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: we are nearly 100%.

asr-000359
00:39:03.020 --> 00:39:05.240
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: However, for tuna and round scud,

asr-000360
00:39:05.740 --> 00:39:08.740
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: we remain below self-sufficiency.

asr-000361
00:39:10.400 --> 00:39:14.220
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Although the department's budget has expanded,

asr-000362
00:39:15.520 --> 00:39:18.840
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: its share in the national budget remains relatively low,

asr-000363
00:39:18.840 --> 00:39:19.840
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: averaging just...

asr-000364
00:39:20.360 --> 00:39:24.980
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: 2.62% over the past two decades.

asr-000365
00:39:25.640 --> 00:39:28.200
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: While comparing it with our Asian neighbor,

asr-000366
00:39:28.980 --> 00:39:31.420
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: FAO data underscores this gap,

asr-000367
00:39:31.520 --> 00:39:34.560
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: showing that agriculture's share of government expenditure

asr-000368
00:39:34.560 --> 00:39:40.380
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: in the Philippines is a lot lower than the expenditures in China,

asr-000369
00:39:40.820 --> 00:39:45.280
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: India, Thailand, Vietnam, Bangladesh, and Cambodia.

asr-000370
00:39:45.280 --> 00:39:50.020
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Looking at Indonesia, by contrast,

asr-000371
00:39:50.360 --> 00:39:55.640
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Indonesia indicates a slightly lower share at 2.6%,

asr-000372
00:39:55.640 --> 00:39:58.280
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: yet maintains a larger agricultural sector

asr-000373
00:39:58.280 --> 00:40:01.640
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: that achieves rice sufficiency in 2025.

asr-000374
00:40:02.700 --> 00:40:07.520
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: This comparison suggests that progress depends not only on spending,

asr-000375
00:40:08.520 --> 00:40:12.220
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: but on effective resource management and productivity conversion.

asr-000376
00:40:12.220 --> 00:40:20.220
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: A key factor that has been Indonesia's focus is agricultural extension since 2020.

asr-000377
00:40:20.360 --> 00:40:27.520
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Demonstrating that robust extension services serve as a vital mechanism

asr-000378
00:40:27.520 --> 00:40:30.880
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: for technology transfer, farmer decision support,

asr-000379
00:40:31.100 --> 00:40:33.660
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and targeted intervention delivery.

asr-000380
00:40:35.800 --> 00:40:43.000
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Before we proceed, Mr. Chair, to FY2027 budget,

asr-000381
00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:46.500
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: we would like to highlight the five key result areas

asr-000382
00:40:46.500 --> 00:40:48.080
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: under the

asr-000383
00:40:48.080 --> 00:40:49.360
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Para sa Masabagmaganan,

asr-000384
00:40:49.360 --> 00:40:49.480
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and the Five Key Result Areas.

asr-000385
00:40:49.480 --> 00:40:49.560
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Under the Para sa Masabagmaganan,

asr-000386
00:40:50.360 --> 00:40:56.900
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: we focus our plans and programs among these key objectives.

asr-000387
00:40:57.900 --> 00:41:01.700
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: The first one is on enhanced productivity.

asr-000388
00:41:03.480 --> 00:41:06.100
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: We need to increase the yield per hectare.

asr-000389
00:41:06.560 --> 00:41:08.920
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: We cannot increase our land area,

asr-000390
00:41:09.220 --> 00:41:11.340
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: but definitely we can increase the yield.

asr-000391
00:41:12.160 --> 00:41:14.240
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: We need to increase income,

asr-000392
00:41:14.240 --> 00:41:18.880
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and that means lowering the cost and increasing the value.

asr-000393
00:41:18.880 --> 00:41:23.560
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: We need to improve food security and proper nutrition.

asr-000394
00:41:23.760 --> 00:41:28.060
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: It is not just producing food, but producing nutritious food.

asr-000395
00:41:29.100 --> 00:41:37.100
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: We need to reduce our dependence on import by increasing or improving self-sufficiency,

asr-000396
00:41:37.940 --> 00:41:44.620
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: and ultimately reduce poverty in the agriculture and fishery sector.

asr-000397
00:41:44.620 --> 00:41:48.320
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: For the next set of presentation, Mr. Chair,

asr-000398
00:41:48.880 --> 00:41:54.700
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: I would like to turn over the floor to Undersecretary Nora Oliveros,

asr-000399
00:41:54.800 --> 00:41:57.520
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: who will cast the financial component of our report.

asr-000400
00:41:57.700 --> 00:41:58.400
DA Undersecretary Asis G. Perez: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000401
00:41:58.960 --> 00:42:01.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead, Yusek Oliveros.

asr-000402
00:42:01.900 --> 00:42:03.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Yusek Aziz Perez.

asr-000403
00:42:04.040 --> 00:42:06.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You now have the floor, Yusek Nora.

asr-000404
00:42:06.960 --> 00:42:07.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead.

asr-000405
00:42:11.740 --> 00:42:13.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Oh, there you go.

asr-000406
00:42:13.680 --> 00:42:14.680
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000407
00:42:15.440 --> 00:42:17.100
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Magandang umaga po sa lahat.

asr-000408
00:42:17.100 --> 00:42:24.460
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Before I proceed to the 2027 budget proposal of the Department of Agriculture,

asr-000409
00:42:24.960 --> 00:42:32.820
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: let me first brief the Committee on the Utilization of the Funds of DA for 2026.

asr-000410
00:42:38.820 --> 00:42:45.260
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Well, this slide presents the utilization status of the Department of Agriculture,

asr-000411
00:42:45.260 --> 00:42:47.060
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: net of attached corporation,

asr-000412
00:42:47.100 --> 00:42:50.300
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: as of September 30, 2026,

asr-000413
00:42:50.580 --> 00:42:55.040
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: covering both current and continuing appropriations.

asr-000414
00:42:55.980 --> 00:43:01.360
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: The Department has received a total allotment of ₱141.5 billion

asr-000415
00:43:01.360 --> 00:43:07.140
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: out of the ₱172 billion total adjusted appropriations.

asr-000416
00:43:07.780 --> 00:43:11.960
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Of this amount, ₱90.4 billion has been obligated,

asr-000417
00:43:12.960 --> 00:43:16.960
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: representing an overall obligation rate of 63.9%.

asr-000418
00:43:17.100 --> 00:43:26.560
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Total disbursements amounted to ₱50.8 billion, equivalent to 56.2% of total obligations.

asr-000419
00:43:27.560 --> 00:43:34.160
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: The majority of the allotment is under current appropriation with an obligation rate of 67%

asr-000420
00:43:34.160 --> 00:43:37.100
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: and a disbursement rate of 58%.

asr-000421
00:43:37.620 --> 00:43:43.320
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: For continuing appropriations, the obligation rate is 43.6%,

asr-000422
00:43:43.320 --> 00:43:46.100
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: while the disbursement rate is 38%.

asr-000423
00:43:47.100 --> 00:43:50.320
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: These figures are being monitored by the Department

asr-000424
00:43:50.320 --> 00:43:54.680
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: and have instructed all heads of the agencies

asr-000425
00:43:54.680 --> 00:43:59.000
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: to draw a catch-up plan for 2026

asr-000426
00:43:59.000 --> 00:44:04.240
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: to ensure the timely utilization and disbursement of the available funds

asr-000427
00:44:04.240 --> 00:44:08.900
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: in accordance with the approved programs and applicable government rules.

asr-000428
00:44:10.120 --> 00:44:11.640
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Next slide, please.

asr-000429
00:44:13.040 --> 00:44:16.680
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: This slide shows the summary by major programs,

asr-000430
00:44:17.100 --> 00:44:22.540
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: representing 82% of the total allotment received by the Department of Agriculture.

asr-000431
00:44:23.720 --> 00:44:28.880
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: The Department of Agriculture's major programs are anchored by high-performing areas

asr-000432
00:44:28.880 --> 00:44:31.000
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: like the Agricultural Credit Program,

asr-000433
00:44:31.660 --> 00:44:35.200
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: which achieve highest obligation and disbursement rate.

asr-000434
00:44:35.920 --> 00:44:40.980
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Key initiatives such as the National Rice Program show strong fund commitment,

asr-000435
00:44:40.980 --> 00:44:45.300
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: though disbursement acceleration is needed across several sectors,

asr-000436
00:44:45.840 --> 00:44:46.720
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Most notably

asr-000437
00:44:46.720 --> 00:44:49.320
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: on foreign-assisted projects where

asr-000438
00:44:49.320 --> 00:44:50.900
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: payments lag behind obligations.

asr-000439
00:44:51.220 --> 00:44:53.160
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Overall, programs with large

asr-000440
00:44:53.160 --> 00:44:55.220
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: budget allocations, such as

asr-000441
00:44:55.220 --> 00:44:57.480
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: locally funded programs continue

asr-000442
00:44:57.480 --> 00:44:59.900
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: to drive the bulk of total spending.

asr-000443
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:12.700
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: We have also an update on the unreleased funds for 2027, one reason why we have low obligation rates and disbursements.

asr-000444
00:45:13.280 --> 00:45:18.340
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Some of these are shown on the next slide.

asr-000445
00:45:18.340 --> 00:45:47.860
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Under the Office of the Secretary, we have a total of 49.7 billion unreleased appropriations as of September 30, 2026, of which 19.8 billion were released in October, namely the funds for the FMR projects amounting to 18.68 billion and the establishment of the Agri-Food Hub project amounting to 500 million pesos.

asr-000446
00:45:48.340 --> 00:45:55.080
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Under the Office of the Secretary, we have a total of 49.7 billion unreleased appropriations.

asr-000447
00:45:55.080 --> 00:46:17.220
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Some of these are for the National Rice Program, the National High Value Crops, the FMR projects, Animal Welfare Supervision and Accreditation Program, Biosecurity for Agriculture and Fishery, Building Sustainable Agriculture and Fishery Enterprises or the SAFE projects,

asr-000448
00:46:18.340 --> 00:46:31.300
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: also under the SAGIP-SACA Act, the requests are all for revision, updating the compilation of the required supporting documents to address the observations raised also by the DBM.

asr-000449
00:46:32.600 --> 00:46:47.900
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Also, unreleased as of September 30 is 22 million for the Cold Storage Expansion Project, the Digital Agriculture Project and 500 million for the establishment of the Agri-Food Hub.

asr-000450
00:46:48.340 --> 00:46:52.240
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: The funds were released, however, in October 2026.

asr-000451
00:46:57.240 --> 00:47:01.600
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: September, yeah, October 2026, Mr. Chair.

asr-000452
00:47:02.500 --> 00:47:08.640
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Yes, this is additional for the Food Hub, additional release, 500 million.

asr-000453
00:47:13.320 --> 00:47:14.000
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Okay.

asr-000454
00:47:18.340 --> 00:47:28.360
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: After September 30, we have received the releases for the Food Hub Project of 500 million.

asr-000455
00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:31.400
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: October, yes.

asr-000456
00:47:31.400 --> 00:47:32.300
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Another one.

asr-000457
00:47:34.320 --> 00:47:37.880
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Yun lang po, after September 30, Food Hub lang po.

asr-000458
00:47:38.500 --> 00:47:46.140
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: So the others are still in, of course, are still ongoing and currently being evaluated by the DBM.

asr-000459
00:47:46.620 --> 00:47:47.400
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: And some of which are still...

asr-000460
00:47:48.340 --> 00:47:55.400
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: And some of which are still ongoing with us because we have to comply for some supporting documents, additional requirements by the DBM, Mr. Chair.

asr-000461
00:48:01.400 --> 00:48:07.300
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Next slide are the unreleased appropriations for some of our attached agencies.

asr-000462
00:48:08.160 --> 00:48:11.900
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: We have also a 250 million pending for the ACPC.

asr-000463
00:48:12.720 --> 00:48:18.120
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Also, we have already submitted the request for this, but we have also to comply to certain...

asr-000464
00:48:18.340 --> 00:48:21.520
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Documentary requirements by the DBM.

asr-000465
00:48:21.980 --> 00:48:30.980
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: We have also another pending by the BIFAR, 407 million for the mobile water treatment and desalination system.

asr-000466
00:48:33.420 --> 00:48:40.320
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: So that's the status of our unreleased appropriations as of September 30, Mr. Chair.

asr-000467
00:48:41.420 --> 00:48:48.120
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Now, may I go to the 2027 features of the DA proposal?

asr-000468
00:48:48.340 --> 00:48:49.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead.

asr-000469
00:48:52.400 --> 00:49:01.400
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: For the agri-sector, which includes the DA, the National Irrigation Administration, and the Department of Agri and Reform,

asr-000470
00:49:01.400 --> 00:49:17.400
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: the total NEP that we have received as of today is 261.7 billion pesos, of which 198 billion is allocated to the Department of Agriculture.

asr-000471
00:49:18.340 --> 00:49:30.180
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: So this represents a decrease in the budget of the DA comparing with the 2026 GAA of around 17 billion pesos.

asr-000472
00:49:30.700 --> 00:49:35.640
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: For the whole sector, it is a decrease of 35.3 billion pesos.

asr-000473
00:49:38.700 --> 00:49:45.300
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Let me go to the details of the 198.4 billion allocated for DA for 2027.

asr-000474
00:49:45.300 --> 00:49:47.980
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: The Department of Agriculture.

asr-000475
00:49:48.340 --> 00:49:58.160
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: As a budget of 198 billion, a decrease of 17.2 billion, or 8%, compared to the 2026 GAA.

asr-000476
00:49:58.160 --> 00:50:03.560
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: The Department's budget is distributed across key expenditure categories.

asr-000477
00:50:04.240 --> 00:50:09.780
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: So we have around 8.3 billion, or 4.2%, for salaries and compensation.

asr-000478
00:50:10.680 --> 00:50:18.160
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: MOE, which receives the highest allocation, at 62.46%, or 123.9%.

asr-000479
00:50:18.340 --> 00:50:26.160
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: These, of course, are funds allocated for the different programs, operations, and services of the DA.

asr-000480
00:50:27.000 --> 00:50:39.360
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Capital outlay of around 33.34%, or 66.2 billion, for infrastructure, facilities, and other investment that benefit our farmers and fisher folk.

asr-000481
00:50:39.360 --> 00:50:48.160
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Now, the next slide shows the budget summary as to the cost structure of the budget.

asr-000482
00:50:48.340 --> 00:51:02.300
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: So this is allocated for, the budget of 198 is allocated for general administration and support services, support to operations, and operations.

asr-000483
00:51:03.300 --> 00:51:11.580
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: So the operations budget is allocated around 156 billion for 2027.

asr-000484
00:51:11.580 --> 00:51:12.740
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Okay.

asr-000485
00:51:15.300 --> 00:51:18.260
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: The bulk of the decrease, however,

asr-000486
00:51:18.340 --> 00:51:30.020
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: for the budget of 20, of the DA for 2027, the bulk of the decrease of around 7.2 billion is particularly on the locally funded projects.

asr-000487
00:51:32.240 --> 00:51:35.760
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Also, we have an increase of 20 billion, no?

asr-000488
00:51:36.040 --> 00:51:42.380
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: We have an increase of 20 billion due to the animal industry development and competitive program.

asr-000489
00:51:45.300 --> 00:51:45.980
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Okay.

asr-000490
00:51:47.200 --> 00:51:47.880
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Okay.

asr-000491
00:51:48.340 --> 00:51:49.700
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Next slide, please.

asr-000492
00:51:49.700 --> 00:52:14.460
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: As we look at the budget for 2027, per attached agencies, we have only an increase allocated for the Philippine Center for Post-Harvest Development and Mechanization,

asr-000493
00:52:14.460 --> 00:52:24.420
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: the Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources, and the Philippine Council for Agriculture and Fisheries.

asr-000494
00:52:24.420 --> 00:52:34.600
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: All other attached agencies of the DA have suffered decrease in the allocation of the 2026 budget.

asr-000495
00:52:36.920 --> 00:52:44.420
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: For the attached corporation, again, there's only one corporation that received an increase in its budget.

asr-000496
00:52:44.420 --> 00:52:48.000
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: And this is for the National Tobacco Administration.

asr-000497
00:52:48.780 --> 00:52:58.440
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: All the seven corporations have received a decrease in their budgets for 2027.

asr-000498
00:52:59.700 --> 00:53:11.380
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Particularly, the Fisheries Development Authority for its construction, rehabilitation, and improvement of fish ports, around 15.89%,

asr-000499
00:53:11.380 --> 00:53:13.740
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: and the Philippine Crop Insurance Corporation.

asr-000500
00:53:14.420 --> 00:53:16.420
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Okay.

asr-000501
00:53:16.420 --> 00:53:16.460
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Okay.

asr-000502
00:53:19.200 --> 00:53:24.200
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: For the banner programs, we look at the budget by the banner programs.

asr-000503
00:53:24.460 --> 00:53:29.040
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: Again, all of the banner programs have received decreases in the budget.

asr-000504
00:53:30.180 --> 00:53:39.860
DA Undersecretary Nora C. Oliveros: The National Rice Program, for example, has received a decrease of around 4.8%,

asr-000505
00:53:39.860 --> 00:53:44.400
