Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Di ba?

asr-001996
01:59:01.900 --> 01:59:02.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hindi pa na,

asr-001997
01:59:02.800 --> 01:59:05.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: hindi pa na reprelish yung groundwater,

asr-001998
01:59:05.980 --> 01:59:07.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: yung aquifer natin.

asr-001999
01:59:07.140 --> 01:59:07.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Di ba?

asr-002000
01:59:07.480 --> 01:59:08.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Nadideplete pa.

asr-002001
01:59:08.480 --> 01:59:09.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That's why we have sinkholes.

asr-002002
01:59:09.820 --> 01:59:12.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, I think this has to be the,

asr-002003
01:59:12.360 --> 01:59:15.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: dapat magkaroon ng convergence ang NIA and DPWH

asr-002004
01:59:15.720 --> 01:59:16.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: so that we will have,

asr-002005
01:59:16.960 --> 01:59:19.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we will be preserving,

asr-002006
01:59:19.440 --> 01:59:22.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we will be retaining more water on dry days.

asr-002007
01:59:22.400 --> 01:59:24.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, thank you for your opinion.

asr-002008
01:59:24.520 --> 01:59:27.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I'm happy that you support this,

asr-002009
01:59:27.820 --> 01:59:30.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and thank you for your support and for the direction.

asr-002010
01:59:30.900 --> 01:59:33.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sabi ko kaya yung mga sabo dams,

asr-002011
01:59:33.140 --> 01:59:36.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: dapat ganoon siguring gawin natin from the upland.

asr-002012
01:59:37.640 --> 01:59:38.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We are cascading,

asr-002013
01:59:39.120 --> 01:59:40.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: mapabagal yung takbo ng tubig,

asr-002014
01:59:40.940 --> 01:59:41.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: pero we retain.

asr-002015
01:59:41.760 --> 01:59:42.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tama, may aquaculture,

asr-002016
01:59:42.920 --> 01:59:44.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: maraming pwedeng gawin for tourism

asr-002017
01:59:44.720 --> 01:59:49.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and even for, of course, for irrigation.

asr-002018
01:59:50.140 --> 01:59:51.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And just like to assume,

asr-002019
01:59:52.280 --> 01:59:53.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: because of our fiscal space,

asr-002020
01:59:53.800 --> 01:59:55.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: very tightly in our fiscal space,

asr-002021
01:59:55.600 --> 01:59:57.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: normally most of the agencies,

asr-002022
01:59:57.360 --> 01:59:59.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: really suffered budget.

