BFAR Director Elizer S. Salilig: Hinaarap ko pa yung...

asr-002087
02:06:09.500 --> 02:06:15.400
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: With the indulgence of our National Director,

asr-002088
02:06:15.400 --> 02:06:17.840
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: we deployed 30-meter vests.

asr-002089
02:06:17.860 --> 02:06:20.860
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: And 50-meter vessels po in the West Philippine Sea.

asr-002090
02:06:21.400 --> 02:06:34.620
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: And then we provided as well boats or fishing boats to our fisher folk for regions 1, 3, and 4B.

asr-002091
02:06:35.240 --> 02:06:44.660
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: So, and then we provided po yung fuel subsidy for all those fisher folk operating on those area, Mr. Chair.

asr-002092
02:06:44.660 --> 02:06:47.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Is that daily?

asr-002093
02:06:47.860 --> 02:06:53.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sabi ko, nagdarasyon tayo ng fuel or may schedule po yan?

asr-002094
02:06:54.000 --> 02:07:01.620
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: Yung fuel po namin, Mr. Chair, bali po, dun lang po sa available na pondo po natin.

asr-002095
02:07:01.740 --> 02:07:11.600
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: But right now, it's good news po that we have this 1 billion pesos for our uplift to be distributed to our fisher folk po.

asr-002096
02:07:11.600 --> 02:07:16.600
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: So, including po yung those fisher folk operating in regions...

asr-002097
02:07:17.860 --> 02:07:21.200
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: 1, 3, and 4B, Mr. Chair.

asr-002098
02:07:23.200 --> 02:07:24.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pero yun pa rin ang ano, no?

asr-002099
02:07:24.360 --> 02:07:27.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That is still one of the richest in marine resources, to.

asr-002100
02:07:28.040 --> 02:07:29.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya talagang...

asr-002101
02:07:29.660 --> 02:07:31.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Doon talaga nangingisahan to.

asr-002102
02:07:31.080 --> 02:07:38.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pero is it true that, ano, almost 21,000 acres of coral reefs already are sa West Philippine Sea area?

asr-002103
02:07:38.900 --> 02:07:40.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ano na, nasira na?

asr-002104
02:07:41.600 --> 02:07:42.660
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: Do you have any news?

asr-002105
02:07:42.660 --> 02:07:45.600
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: With that, Your Honor, we don't have the assessment yet.

asr-002106
02:07:45.600 --> 02:07:47.600
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: But, of course, with the...

asr-002107
02:07:47.860 --> 02:07:51.780
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: deployment of our vessel, we can...

asr-002108
02:07:51.780 --> 02:07:53.360
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: pretty sure that we can assess the area.

asr-002109
02:07:53.940 --> 02:07:58.180
BFAR Assistant Director for Administrative and Other Support Services Zaldy P. Perez: But, of course, considering that there's no harassment at all, Mr. Chair.

asr-002110
02:08:01.320 --> 02:08:04.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Actually, I want to ask naman sa farm-to-market roads.

asr-002111
02:08:07.120 --> 02:08:11.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: For 2013, the DA is proposing 16 billion for farm-to-market roads.

asr-002112
02:08:11.480 --> 02:08:16.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Bawat taon, iniulat kung ilang kilometre na kalsada ang natapos.

asr-002113
02:08:17.860 --> 02:08:20.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sa kanatilang magsasakaba talaga ang nakikinabang.

asr-002114
02:08:20.380 --> 02:08:25.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, taon-taon din kasi may mga balita pa rin tukol sa mga gulay at iba pang ani na nabubulok

asr-002115
02:08:25.920 --> 02:08:29.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: at tinatapo na lang at hindi maibenta sa maayos na presyo.

asr-002116
02:08:30.020 --> 02:08:32.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, malaki yung papel ng middleman.

asr-002117
02:08:32.960 --> 02:08:34.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, question.

asr-002118
02:08:34.580 --> 02:08:38.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, for next year, sa farm-to-market road,

asr-002119
02:08:38.020 --> 02:08:46.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: how many kilometres is ang natin ang intended to construct for next year?

asr-002120
02:08:47.860 --> 02:08:50.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, yung sa 16 billion, 16 billion na ba?

asr-002121
02:08:50.600 --> 02:09:01.200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, yung sa 16 billion na yun, 1,100, almost 1,100 kilometres, sir, ang farm-to-market road.

asr-002122
02:09:03.440 --> 02:09:10.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And, also, I'd like to touch on yung sa cold storage, Secretary.

asr-002123
02:09:11.600 --> 02:09:16.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In 2025, the cold storage expansion project reported disbursed only 1.4% of its

asr-002124
02:09:17.860 --> 02:09:18.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: allocation.

asr-002125
02:09:18.620 --> 02:09:22.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, of course, alam nyo naman ngayon, masikip.

asr-002126
02:09:22.500 --> 02:09:28.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, we would, we want to make sure that this is all utilized and dispersed, yung mga pondo.

asr-002127
02:09:29.640 --> 02:09:33.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ayaw natin maglagay ng hindi magagamit ngayon dahil nga sa sikip.

asr-002128
02:09:34.160 --> 02:09:38.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, what caused the delays and how many cold storage facilities have actually been completed

asr-002129
02:09:38.620 --> 02:09:40.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and made operational?

asr-002130
02:09:41.240 --> 02:09:43.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, siguro, yun muna.

asr-002131
02:09:43.020 --> 02:09:47.560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: I admit that we had a slow start.

asr-002132
02:09:47.860 --> 02:09:53.060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa aming mga cold storage projects due to technical design issues.

asr-002133
02:09:54.080 --> 02:09:59.380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But, fortunately, tamang-tama lang po yung tanong ninyo.

asr-002134
02:10:00.720 --> 02:10:05.560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tuloy-tuloy na namin inaugurate yung mga cold storage facilities na tinatayo.

asr-002135
02:10:05.560 --> 02:10:15.040
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Actually, I was just in Camarines Sur and we turned over four setups already.

asr-002136
02:10:16.500 --> 02:10:17.560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Earlier this year, we inaugurated.

asr-002137
02:10:17.860 --> 02:10:21.260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: We inaugurated our first mega cold storage in Pili, Kamsur.

asr-002138
02:10:22.020 --> 02:10:26.300
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung sa Taguig na cold storage natin should be completed by middle of next year.

asr-002139
02:10:27.200 --> 02:10:31.660
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Cabanatuan will be, mega cold storage will be completed by next year.

asr-002140
02:10:32.340 --> 02:10:35.640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: San Jose, Mindoro, and ano pa isa?

asr-002141
02:10:36.180 --> 02:10:38.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang malaking bagay for the onions, ano?

asr-002142
02:10:38.020 --> 02:10:40.560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: San Jose, Mindoro, isang mega.

asr-002143
02:10:41.200 --> 02:10:42.420
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tsaka, ano yung katabi niya?

asr-002144
02:10:43.620 --> 02:10:45.580
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa Sablayan, Mindoro also.

asr-002145
02:10:46.360 --> 02:10:47.020
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa Manolo Fortich.

asr-002146
02:10:47.860 --> 02:10:50.560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa Sablayan lang, magtatayo rin tayo ng isang cold storage na malaki.

asr-002147
02:10:51.240 --> 02:10:59.760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At total modular cold storage natin is about 70 units of which tuloy-tuloy na ho yung turnover niya.

asr-002148
02:10:59.760 --> 02:11:13.500
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So, pumilis na ho at I'm happy to note that medyo yung farmer beneficiaries natin quite happy na meron na silang solar powered and wind powered battery storage, Mr. Chair.

asr-002149
02:11:14.180 --> 02:11:16.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Well, that's good news for our local production, Secretary.

asr-002150
02:11:17.860 --> 02:11:30.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Let me move on to, ano, of course, that one, another sector that is close to my heart because coming from Negros, I saw Sir Paul Alcaza Ascona here, SRA.

asr-002151
02:11:31.840 --> 02:11:38.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: My mother coming from, who hails from Negros, of course, sugar industry is very close to us.

asr-002152
02:11:39.040 --> 02:11:41.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: SIDA has a mandated annual funding allocation under the law.

asr-002153
02:11:41.920 --> 02:11:47.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yet funding has always fallen short. Under the 2027 NEP, 1 billion

asr-002154
02:11:47.520 --> 02:11:51.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: is allocated to the SRA with the limited budget of SIDA.

asr-002155
02:11:51.840 --> 02:12:01.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How can we ensure that the full intended budget for SIDA programs is actually released and properly utilized to help our sugar cane farmers?

asr-002156
02:12:01.380 --> 02:12:02.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro pwede nga na?

asr-002157
02:12:02.580 --> 02:12:07.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Si ating SRA administrator will take advantage of your presence.

asr-002158
02:12:09.120 --> 02:12:10.360
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002159
02:12:10.680 --> 02:12:12.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Senator JV.

asr-002161
02:12:13.080 --> 02:12:13.720
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Yeah.

asr-002162
02:12:14.340 --> 02:12:16.200
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So, so far, for the last...

asr-002163
02:12:17.860 --> 02:12:25.340
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Prior to 2022, our SIDA budget went down to as low as 300 million, 500 million.

asr-002164
02:12:25.620 --> 02:12:27.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, I asked, pero 2 billion niya nung muna na.

asr-002165
02:12:27.940 --> 02:12:28.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes.

asr-002166
02:12:28.260 --> 02:12:29.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: On the first year po, sir.

asr-002167
02:12:30.060 --> 02:12:32.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Because it was not utilized, it went down to 500.

asr-002168
02:12:32.760 --> 02:12:34.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Now, low as 300.

asr-002169
02:12:34.200 --> 02:12:35.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So now, it's back to 1 billion.

asr-002170
02:12:36.020 --> 02:12:37.200
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Yes po, Mr. Chair.

asr-002171
02:12:37.280 --> 02:12:39.060
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: For the last three years po, 1 billion.

asr-002172
02:12:39.260 --> 02:12:42.860
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: And then this year, yung alam ko po is 1 billion ulit.

asr-002173
02:12:43.540 --> 02:12:44.620
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: We have...

asr-002174
02:12:44.620 --> 02:12:46.860
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: We have carried over...

asr-002175
02:12:47.860 --> 02:12:52.060
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: I think almost 500 million kasi na-unutilized ever since before.

asr-002176
02:12:52.760 --> 02:12:57.460
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: And for the last three years, we've tried our best to spend yung previous po.

asr-002177
02:12:57.880 --> 02:13:02.700
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So, we've been spending over 1 billion for the last two years.

asr-002178
02:13:02.700 --> 02:13:10.240
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: And hopefully, if given 2 billion, we will be able to fully utilize it, Mr. Chair.

asr-002179
02:13:10.860 --> 02:13:11.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, sir.

asr-002180
02:13:11.280 --> 02:13:13.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We're hoping that it will be...

asr-002181
02:13:13.980 --> 02:13:17.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It will be used effectively and maximized.

asr-002182
02:13:17.860 --> 02:13:22.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siyempre, tayo, ano eh, I'm the author of the Sugarcane Industry Development Act

asr-002183
02:13:22.640 --> 02:13:28.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: with the intent of reviving the sugar industry of Negros.

asr-002184
02:13:29.060 --> 02:13:37.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang ano lang na, how about dun sa ano, how is the RSS affecting our sugar production?

asr-002185
02:13:37.200 --> 02:13:40.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Talagang minsan, hindi tayo inaabot ng swerte sa sugar industry.

asr-002186
02:13:40.940 --> 02:13:42.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tinamaan pa tayo ng peste, no?

asr-002187
02:13:42.360 --> 02:13:46.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, how is the sugar industry coping with it now?

asr-002188
02:13:47.860 --> 02:13:48.620
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-002189
02:13:48.620 --> 02:13:55.620
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So far, our production in 2024-2025 was...

asr-002190
02:13:55.620 --> 02:14:00.040
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Since 2022-2025, we've been growing, actually, in production.

asr-002191
02:14:00.780 --> 02:14:05.240
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Our peak happened in 2024-2025, we produced over 2 million tons.

asr-002192
02:14:05.960 --> 02:14:14.280
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: And then, in 2025-2026, because of El Nino and the onset of RSS IPO,

asr-002193
02:14:14.280 --> 02:14:17.380
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: we went down to 1.85.

asr-002194
02:14:17.860 --> 02:14:27.440
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: And this year, in anticipation for the drastic decrease in rainfall on a year-on-year comparison,

asr-002195
02:14:28.160 --> 02:14:32.280
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: our estimated production is down to 1.6 million.

asr-002196
02:14:32.500 --> 02:14:34.520
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: And that's fighting RSSI as well.

asr-002197
02:14:36.540 --> 02:14:41.800
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: RSSI po kasi, Mr. Chair, is not part of any budget, even SIDA.

asr-002198
02:14:42.300 --> 02:14:45.680
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: SIDA kasi po is pre-allocated to certain items only.

asr-002199
02:14:45.680 --> 02:14:47.680
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: And we hope and pray to the...

asr-002200
02:14:47.860 --> 02:14:56.580
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Committee and to the Chairman po, sana, that we can have additional budget to fight this new pest, RSSI,

asr-002201
02:14:56.760 --> 02:15:00.020
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: which we never anticipated for Mr. Chair.

asr-002202
02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:02.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But how are we coping with it?

asr-002203
02:15:03.500 --> 02:15:07.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Meron na tayong solution for fighting the RSSI?

asr-002204
02:15:08.120 --> 02:15:14.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And also, were we able to provide assistance to the sugarcane farmers?

asr-002205
02:15:15.600 --> 02:15:20.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And how many in anticipation of the RSSI and may super-el-lino pa?

asr-002206
02:15:21.140 --> 02:15:25.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So that we can prepare already, syempre as budget chair, as finance chair, I would like to find out.

asr-002207
02:15:25.820 --> 02:15:33.140
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Yes. Mr. Chair, for the initial first year po of RSSI in Negros,

asr-002208
02:15:34.140 --> 02:15:42.140
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: SRA from its meager corporate budget po spent about 188 million in assistance to farmers.

asr-002209
02:15:42.500 --> 02:15:47.320
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: This includes chemicals, fertilizer, and others, among others.

asr-002210
02:15:47.800 --> 02:15:51.740
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: And from SIDA, we were able to utilize about 28 million.

asr-002211
02:15:52.180 --> 02:15:54.800
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So it's a total of 209 million.

asr-002212
02:15:54.800 --> 02:15:55.800
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Now for this year...

asr-002213
02:15:56.780 --> 02:16:00.920
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: The DA extended 35 million directly to LGUs

asr-002214
02:16:00.920 --> 02:16:07.080
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: because we had issues on how to fight RSSI with the province and the other agencies.

asr-002215
02:16:07.900 --> 02:16:11.040
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So there's 35 million directly to LGUs.

asr-002216
02:16:11.800 --> 02:16:20.700
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: And I think a total of 400-something million of assistance to farmers and farm workers po

asr-002217
02:16:20.700 --> 02:16:25.660
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: at 10,000 per farmer or per worker po through DSWD po.

asr-002218
02:16:25.820 --> 02:16:28.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, just a...

asr-002219
02:16:28.160 --> 02:16:35.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anyway, I'm hoping that we'll be able to overcome this RSSI problem and super-el-lino.

asr-002220
02:16:35.440 --> 02:16:37.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But nonetheless, I'm also...

asr-002221
02:16:38.280 --> 02:16:44.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung commitment also of the SRA that the timing of the importation will now be...

asr-002222
02:16:46.000 --> 02:16:50.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Will not coincide with the harvest season.

asr-002223
02:16:50.640 --> 02:16:52.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, kasi konti na rin ikikitain nila.

asr-002224
02:16:52.800 --> 02:16:53.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, huwag na natin sasabayan.

asr-002225
02:16:54.060 --> 02:16:54.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dapat na lang.

asr-002226
02:16:54.800 --> 02:16:55.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We understand.

asr-002227
02:16:55.820 --> 02:16:57.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: of all of these factors

asr-002228
02:16:57.780 --> 02:16:59.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: that we need to import also because of the

asr-002229
02:16:59.760 --> 02:17:02.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: shortage but yung timing na lang

asr-002230
02:17:02.120 --> 02:17:03.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I'm hoping that we can get

asr-002231
02:17:03.700 --> 02:17:05.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: your commitment that

asr-002232
02:17:05.380 --> 02:17:06.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: SRA will

asr-002233
02:17:06.680 --> 02:17:09.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: only issue

asr-002234
02:17:09.060 --> 02:17:11.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: authority to import

asr-002235
02:17:11.440 --> 02:17:13.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: not during harvest season.

asr-002236
02:17:14.720 --> 02:17:15.480
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Mr. Chair,

asr-002237
02:17:15.480 --> 02:17:16.680
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: yes, I think

asr-002238
02:17:16.680 --> 02:17:19.400
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: the Secretary po and the

asr-002239
02:17:19.400 --> 02:17:21.520
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: SRA are committed to

asr-002240
02:17:21.520 --> 02:17:23.440
