asr-004796
04:16:43.140 --> 04:16:43.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Last mile.

asr-004797
04:16:44.800 --> 04:16:50.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They were able to address even the last mile because they had economies of scale and they had volume.

asr-004798
04:16:51.640 --> 04:16:54.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And only the private sector can really do,

asr-004799
04:16:54.040 --> 04:16:57.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: they can really do PPP in bulk, di ba?

asr-004800
04:16:58.860 --> 04:16:59.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-004801
04:16:59.840 --> 04:17:04.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, we hope, we hope that moving forward, ganoon ang magiging direksyon natin.

asr-004802
04:17:07.520 --> 04:17:08.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-004803
04:17:10.340 --> 04:17:10.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So,

asr-004804
04:17:12.860 --> 04:17:14.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: anong isa?

asr-004805
04:17:15.480 --> 04:17:19.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yung issue sa ating corn, kasi feeds, di ba?

asr-004806
04:17:19.520 --> 04:17:21.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yung, yung MAV.

asr-004807
04:17:23.400 --> 04:17:23.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-004808
04:17:24.040 --> 04:17:24.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Can you clarify this?

asr-004809
04:17:25.040 --> 04:17:26.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because yung concern dito is,

asr-004810
04:17:27.780 --> 04:17:32.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: although mas mataas yung ating corn stocks,

asr-004811
04:17:32.400 --> 04:17:39.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: according to PSA, 47% increase compared to last year,

asr-004812
04:17:41.640 --> 04:17:48.300
